    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="26">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 26</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.d"/><pb n="510–511" ed="#liebermann"/>De quatre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.e"/> chemins, ceo est a saveir Watling<hi rend="italic">e</hi>strete<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.3"/>, Er[m]ing<hi rend="italic">e</hi>strete, Fosse, Hykenild<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.e"/>, ki en aucun de ces quatre chemins ocist aucun, ki seit errant par le pais, u asaut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.4"/>, si enfreint la<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.5"/> pais le rei.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.16"/><pb n="510–511" ed="#liebermann"/>De III<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.a"/> chemins, ço est a saveir Wetlingstrete<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.17"/> et Ermingestrete<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.18"/> et Fos, ki en alcun de ces chemins occit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.19"/> home, qui seit errant per le pais, u asalt, si enfrei[n]t<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.20"/> la pais le rei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.21"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="510–511" ed="#liebermann"/>De tribus stratis regiis. In tribus stratis regiis, id est Watelingestrete, Erningestrete<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.1"/> et Fosse, qui hominem per patriam transeuntem occiderit uel assultum fecerit, pacem regis infringit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="26" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="266" ed="#robertson"/>De quatre chemins, ceo est a saver Watlingestrete, Er[m]ingestrete, Fosse, Hykenild, ki en aucun de ces quatre chemins ocist aucun ki seit errant par le pais, u asaut, si enfreint la pais le rei.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="510–511" ed="#liebermann"/>26.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#missing"/> Von den 3 (4 <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>) [Reichs]strassen, d. h. nämlich Wætlingstrasse, Erminstrasse, Fosse (Ikenilde <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>): wer auf einer dieser (4 <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>) Strassen jemanden, der über Land reist, tödtet oder angreift, so bricht er den königlichen Sonderfrieden.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">26. Of the 3 (4 <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>) [royal] roads, i.e. namely Wætling Street, Ermine Street, Fosse (Ikenild <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>): whoever on one of these (4 <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi>) roads kills or attacks someone travelling across country, he breaks the royal special peace.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="267" ed="#robertson"/>If anyone slays or assaults anyone who is travelling through the country on any of the (following) four highways, namely, Watling Street, Ermine Street, the Fosse Way, the Icknield Way, he violates the King's Peace.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="511">ECf 12c</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">vgl. E Cf. 12c</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="409"><label>overlaps</label> ECf <quote>Overlaps with Leges Edwardi Confessoris included Peter's Pence and the peace of the four great roads</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 266–267 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 510–511, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">De treis ch. <hi rend="italic">nimmt als Rubrik MAT.; aber Text begann nicht</hi> ceo, <hi rend="italic">eher</hi> ki</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">MAT. take De treis ch. as the rubric; but the text did not begin with ceo, rather with ki</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">die vierte Strasse fehlt IL; wenn dies archaischer ist, so entnahm sie Hk vielleicht</hi> E Cf. 12, <hi rend="italic">den er wenige Seiten weiter copirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the fourth road is missing in IL; if this is the more archaic reading, Hk perhaps took it from E Cf. 12, which he copies a few pages further on</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Watling'st., Erning'st. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi> [<hi rend="italic">vgl. L</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Watling'st., Erning'st. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi> [<hi rend="italic">cf. L</hi>]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nicht</hi> assaut</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not assaut</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">le <hi rend="italic">falsch TO.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">le wrongly TO.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so auch L</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so also L</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XXX. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XXX. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-eete <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> Wetleings. <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-eete <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> Wetleings. <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ermings. <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ermings. <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">oceit <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">oceit <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">enfreit <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">enfreit <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">510</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">roi <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">roi <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">511</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ermi. <hi rend="italic">bessert Thorpe; aber vgl. Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Thorpe emends to Ermi.; but cf. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_26.lnote.de.1__2" n="1. 2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">290</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Königsschutz 8; Handfrieden 7a C; Strassen 4. 7—9g ff. 11a. Über ihren Lauf <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>. jetzt Haverfield in <hi rend="italic">Cambridge med. hist</hi>. I (1911) 376; zum Icknieldway Round <hi rend="italic">Great roll of the Pipe for 1184/5</hi> (1913); zur Fosse: Major <hi rend="italic">Early wars of Wessex</hi> 41</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Königsschutz 8; Handfrieden 7a C; Strassen 4. 7—9g ff. 11a. On their course <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> now Haverfield in <hi rend="italic">Cambridge med. hist</hi>. I (1911) 376; on the Icknieldway, Round <hi rend="italic">Great roll of the Pipe for 1184/5</hi> (1913); on the Fosse: Major <hi rend="italic">Early wars of Wessex</hi> 41</seg></note>
      </div>
